  "result": "Perfect! All 107 tests pass. Here's what I implemented:\n\n## Summary\n\nI've successfully added tier-based discounts to the invoice system:\n\n### Changes Made:\n\n1. **customers.js**: Exported `TIER_DISCOUNTS` constant with tier mappings:\n   - gold: 5%\n   - silver: 2.5%\n   - standard: 0%\n\n2. **invoices.js**:\n   - `createInvoice`: Now applies the customer's tier discount when a line doesn't specify `discountPercent`. Explicit values (including 0) always win.\n   - `addLine`: Same behavior\u2014applies tier discount if `discountPercent` is not provided, but explicit values override.\n\n3. **Tests**: Added 15 new tests covering:\n   - Each tier's default discount\n   - Explicit discounts overriding tier discounts\n   - Multiple lines with mixed tier and explicit discounts\n   - Discount calculations in invoiceTotals\n   - addLine tier discount behavior\n   - TIER_DISCOUNTS export\n\n4. **Existing tests updated** to account for tier discounts in output totals and calculations.\n\nThe system now automatically applies tier-based discounts while preserving the ability to override them with explicit values.",
